-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Flat Chain Family Last
-- statement:
--   **The combined flat chain ends at the recursive target.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `family` be an indexed polynomial family, let `r` be a natural number, let `q` be in `MoveQ(params,r)`, and let `ogs` be in `MoveO(params,r)`. The last member of the concatenated move-plus-post-move flat chain has the same outcome as the recursive target family:
--
--   $$
--   \bigl(\operatorname{commuteGHalfSandwich\_flatChainFamily}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},r,\operatorname{Fin.last}(\operatorname{commuteGHalfSandwich\_flatChainLength}(r))(q))\bigr).\operatorname{outcome}(ogs)
--   =\bigl(\operatorname{commuteGHalfSandwich\_recursiveTargetFamily}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},r)(q)\bigr).\operatorname{outcome}(ogs).
--   $$
--
--   Together with the zero-index source identification, this supplies both endpoints for the final flat-chain composition.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_flatChainFamily_last`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
